Finding
-------
8 wrapped call(s), 46 authored config elements, mean 5.8 per call.

Each element is a decision a human made and a future reader must
re-derive. None of it is recoverable from the binary, because the
binary does not describe itself.

Here (R-SIM-4): adasManifest() names every port and its schema, so
the equivalent cost is 0 -- `sim probe <lib>` prints the port set
and the pipeline wires by name. The cost above is paid only by
`impl: legacy:` stages, for binaries that cannot carry a manifest.

R-SIM-15 consequence: the override grammar stays CLOSED at four
verbs. The rules measured above are what an open grammar becomes.
